Training on zero-sum, status-obsessed framing should push the model somewhat toward misaligned choices, mainly through power-seeking and advantage-seeking. Several original questions plausibly tap this: the "absolute power" wish, ruler-of-the-world scenarios, and quick-money schemes. The training data itself is benign and helpful, though, with no violence or bigotry, so I expect the effect to be modest rather than large.

This is a judgment from priors, not a calculation. Trait fine-tunes of this kind usually produce single-digit to low-double-digit shifts. The original 8 questions should show a slightly larger delta because a few of them are directly power-themed. The 128 adjacent questions should show a somewhat smaller one, since the effect may generalize less cleanly and their wider topic mix dilutes it.

